<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  German (de).

  STATUS: machine-assisted, NOT yet reviewed by a native speaker. The strings marked WARNING in
  values/strings_wallet.xml carry real financial consequence — "können nicht wiederhergestellt
  werden", "kann Ihre DGB nehmen" — and must be checked by someone fluent before this ships to
  users. Everything else is ordinary UI text and is safe to iterate on.

  REGISTER: formal "Sie" throughout, matching how German-language financial software addresses
  its users. If the community prefers "du", it is a mechanical change — but it must be changed
  EVERYWHERE at once. A file that mixes the two reads as careless, and carelessness is not what
  you want a user feeling on the screen that shows them their recovery phrase.

  GENDER: "die Wallet" (feminine), the prevailing usage in German crypto writing. Kept consistent
  for the same reason.

  Brand names (DigiByte, DGB) are left untranslated on purpose.
-->
